Root cause:
The free_irq() call in mpu3050_common_remove() incorrectly passed the device structure (mpu3050) instead of the trigger structure (mpu3050->trig) as the handler context, which mismatches the registration and leads to potential issues.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
free_irq(mpu3050->irq, mpu3050);
Reason:
The free_irq() call uses the device structure (`mpu3050`) as the handler context, but the IRQ was registered with `mpu3050->trig` (the trigger structure) as the context. This mismatch can cause undefined behavior or failure to properly release the IRQ.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
free_irq(mpu3050->irq, mpu3050->trig);
Reason:
The corrected free_irq() call passes the same trigger structure that was used during IRQ registration, ensuring proper cleanup and matching the context.


